{"term":"prize","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:4a59905e6942dbfc75","definition":"That which is taken from another; something captured; a thing seized by force, stratagem, or superior power.","example":"[…] wherefore he now begunne\nTo challenge her anew, as his owne prize,\nWhom formerly he had in battell wonne,","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["price","prise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prize#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a09c1e30713047a288","definition":"Anything captured by a belligerent using the rights of war; especially, property captured at sea in virtue of the rights of war, as a vessel.","example":"Having taken all the Treasure on Board their own Ships, and plundered their Prize of every Thing elſe they either wanted or liked, they let her go; ſhe not being able to continue her Voyage, returned back: […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["price","prise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prize#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c17013768b7bd7bba3","definition":"An honour or reward striven for in a competitive contest; anything offered to be competed for, or as an inducement to, or reward of, effort.","example":"I fought and conquer’d, yet have lost the prize.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["price","prise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prize#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7bbc218b469854f069","definition":"That which may be won by chance, as in a lottery.","example":"Cecil Rhodes […] was never tired of impressing upon one that the fact of being an Englishman was “the greatest prize in the lottery of life,” and that it was that thought which always sustained him when he was troubled.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["price","prise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prize#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a7ba10dab5f2c096d1","definition":"Anything worth striving for; a valuable possession held or in prospect.","example":"I press toward the mark for the prize of the high calling of God in Christ Jesus.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["price","prise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prize#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4ab7cc463a057ba20f","definition":"A contest for a reward; competition.","example":"Like one of two contending in a prize,\nThat thinks he hath done well in people's eyes […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["price","prise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prize#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6b5fc8fcdad94bc9b7","definition":"A lever; a pry; also, the hold of a lever.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["prise"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["price","prise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prize#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:25f3e663dd65aa2b7d","definition":"To consider highly valuable; to esteem.","example":"[…] I\nBeyond 